1
00:00:09,259 --> 00:00:10,593
<i>‎Jung Won-young</i>

2
00:00:10,677 --> 00:00:14,139
<i>‎is the 12th player</i>
<i>‎to be eliminated from </i>‎The Devil's Plan.

3
00:00:15,056 --> 00:00:17,142
<i>‎Jang Dong-min, the first-place player,</i>

4
00:00:17,225 --> 00:00:18,977
<i>‎will be rewarded with four Pieces.</i>

5
00:00:19,060 --> 00:00:20,937
‎How did he get all of them right?

6
00:00:21,021 --> 00:00:22,355
‎-He's too much.
‎-Congrats.

7
00:00:22,439 --> 00:00:23,732
<i>‎Based on the rankings,</i>

8
00:00:23,815 --> 00:00:26,067
<i>‎players in first and second place</i>
<i>‎will go to the living area,</i>

9
00:00:26,985 --> 00:00:30,905
<i>‎and players in third through fifth</i>
<i>‎will go to prison.</i>

10
00:00:30,989 --> 00:00:32,407
‎-Let's go.
‎-Come on.

11
00:00:32,490 --> 00:00:36,244
<i>‎Now, please make your way</i>
<i>‎to your respective living spaces.</i>

12
00:00:36,327 --> 00:00:38,872
‎Warden, it's been a while.

13
00:00:38,955 --> 00:00:40,582
‎Do you remember me?

14
00:00:40,665 --> 00:00:43,543
‎Sorry, I have nothing.
‎I left it all behind.

15
00:00:43,626 --> 00:00:45,670
‎Honestly, I was on edge the whole time.

16
00:00:45,754 --> 00:00:47,380
‎-I wasn't at all confident.
‎-Right.

17
00:00:47,964 --> 00:00:50,341
‎-Good job today.
‎-You too.

18
00:00:50,842 --> 00:00:52,302
‎-Welcome.
‎-Welcome back.

19
00:00:52,385 --> 00:00:53,720
‎-Did they save my spot?
‎-Welcome.

20
00:00:53,803 --> 00:00:54,804
‎Welcome home, to be exact.

21
00:00:54,888 --> 00:00:56,806
‎-Welcome.
‎-My gosh, this place…

22
00:00:56,890 --> 00:00:59,142
‎JAE JAE is an OG member too.

23
00:00:59,225 --> 00:01:00,727
‎Totally.

24
00:01:00,810 --> 00:01:03,021
‎-We have only the OGs left.
‎-We were the first to be here.

25
00:01:03,104 --> 00:01:04,230
‎-Team Greater Good.
‎-Yeah.

26
00:01:04,856 --> 00:01:05,857
‎Team Greater Good.

27
00:01:06,733 --> 00:01:09,402
‎When you're in the exile zone,
‎you don't know what's up

28
00:01:09,486 --> 00:01:11,488
‎until the main match ends
‎and new people join us.

29
00:01:11,571 --> 00:01:12,864
‎Every time someone showed up,

30
00:01:12,947 --> 00:01:15,533
‎I was glad you two managed to survive.

31
00:01:16,034 --> 00:01:18,286
‎-We've been through a lot.
‎-We hung on for dear life.

32
00:01:18,369 --> 00:01:21,539
‎I was worried that there might be people
‎I'm not really close with here,

33
00:01:21,623 --> 00:01:24,542
<i>‎but here I am</i>
<i>‎with all the original members.</i>

34
00:01:24,626 --> 00:01:26,544
‎I'm so at ease here.

35
00:01:26,628 --> 00:01:28,213
‎I'm just the king of prison.

36
00:01:28,296 --> 00:01:30,298
‎We have the queen
‎of the exile zone now too.

37
00:01:30,381 --> 00:01:33,510
<i>‎Today's prison match</i>
<i>‎is gonna be the most intense one yet.</i>

38
00:01:33,593 --> 00:01:37,138
<i>‎XITSUH honestly does well in every game.</i>

39
00:01:37,222 --> 00:01:39,015
<i>‎And who knows</i>

40
00:01:39,098 --> 00:01:42,685
<i>‎what JAE JAE has been through?</i>

41
00:01:42,769 --> 00:01:44,062
‎I can't let my guard down.

42
00:01:44,145 --> 00:01:46,397
‎All right, so tell us. What happened?

43
00:01:46,481 --> 00:01:47,315
‎I'm so curious.

44
00:01:47,398 --> 00:01:49,400
‎-So…
‎-Where should I begin?

45
00:01:49,484 --> 00:01:50,860
‎What do you eat there?

46
00:01:50,944 --> 00:01:52,946
‎It's actually better there.

47
00:01:53,738 --> 00:01:54,781
‎That's infuriating.

48
00:01:54,864 --> 00:01:55,865
‎-I mean…
‎-Damn it.

49
00:01:55,949 --> 00:01:57,700
‎The baguettes have filling.

50
00:01:58,535 --> 00:02:00,411
‎-It's not that amazing.
‎-And breakfast?

51
00:02:00,495 --> 00:02:01,621
‎What do you get for breakfast?

52
00:02:01,704 --> 00:02:05,375
‎They change up the filling slightly
‎for breakfast, lunch, and dinner.

53
00:02:05,458 --> 00:02:06,543
‎It's baguettes nonstop?

54
00:02:06,626 --> 00:02:07,877
‎-Yeah.
‎-That's rough too.

55
00:02:07,961 --> 00:02:09,045
‎-Yeah, it is.
‎-Right.

56
00:02:09,129 --> 00:02:12,549
‎-That might actually be worse.
‎-It's nice at first after staying here.

57
00:02:12,632 --> 00:02:15,218
‎Then you start getting sick of it
‎on day two.

58
00:02:15,301 --> 00:02:17,595
‎I can imagine.
‎You were there for four days, right?

59
00:02:17,679 --> 00:02:18,596
‎Two, three, four…

60
00:02:18,680 --> 00:02:20,348
‎-Saturday, Sunday, Monday…
‎-Three nights.

61
00:02:20,431 --> 00:02:22,016
‎Yeah, you're right.

62
00:02:22,100 --> 00:02:23,309
‎Three whole nights.

63
00:02:23,393 --> 00:02:25,395
‎Then how did you make it back?

64
00:02:25,478 --> 00:02:27,605
‎I managed to accomplish
‎the hidden mission.

65
00:02:27,689 --> 00:02:28,523
‎Which was?

66
00:02:28,606 --> 00:02:29,607
‎A magic square.

67
00:02:30,108 --> 00:02:33,278
‎So will the last person standing
‎in the exile zone be joining us too?

68
00:02:33,361 --> 00:02:35,071
‎-Possibly.
‎-Right?

69
00:02:36,322 --> 00:02:39,868
‎I didn't just come out and say it,
‎but they figured it out.

70
00:02:39,951 --> 00:02:41,911
‎I tried to hide it, but I failed.

71
00:02:42,412 --> 00:02:43,788
‎I'm so curious.

72
00:02:43,872 --> 00:02:44,956
‎I'm sure.

73
00:02:45,039 --> 00:02:46,207
‎I really am.

74
00:02:47,208 --> 00:02:50,170
‎It really feels like I'm dreaming.

75
00:02:50,253 --> 00:02:53,965
‎The important part is that
‎even if you get eliminated,

76
00:02:54,048 --> 00:02:55,633
‎you get a second chance.

77
00:02:55,717 --> 00:02:58,928
‎Since that's the case,
‎whoever comes on top

78
00:02:59,012 --> 00:03:01,973
‎in tomorrow's redemption match
‎might be joining us too.

79
00:03:02,056 --> 00:03:04,058
‎-One more person got eliminated today.
‎-Right.

80
00:03:04,142 --> 00:03:07,770
‎The final winner among them
‎will be coming back.

81
00:03:07,854 --> 00:03:10,815
<i>‎Well, in a way, it's one more safety net.</i>

82
00:03:10,899 --> 00:03:12,525
‎Up until now, anyway.

83
00:03:12,609 --> 00:03:14,861
‎Tomorrow's the last day,
‎so I assume that'll be gone.

84
00:03:14,944 --> 00:03:17,906
‎Won-young has experienced everything.

85
00:03:17,989 --> 00:03:19,949
<i>‎The hidden mission,</i>

86
00:03:20,033 --> 00:03:22,285
<i>‎the prison, the living area,</i>

87
00:03:22,368 --> 00:03:23,536
‎and the exile zone.

88
00:03:23,620 --> 00:03:24,621
‎You're right.

89
00:03:24,704 --> 00:03:27,123
‎I was so freaked out
‎because we saw that book yesterday.

90
00:03:27,206 --> 00:03:29,250
<i>‎-Letters From Exile.</i>
‎-You mean <i>‎Letters From Exile?</i>

91
00:03:29,334 --> 00:03:31,002
‎LETTERS FROM EXILE

92
00:03:31,586 --> 00:03:33,046
‎Maybe there's a hint in here.

93
00:03:34,297 --> 00:03:35,840
<i>‎When I went to the bookshelf,</i>

94
00:03:35,924 --> 00:03:38,551
<i>‎I noticed every single book</i>
<i>‎was part of a series.</i>

95
00:03:38,635 --> 00:03:42,222
<i>‎Each book had its own group except one.</i>

96
00:03:42,305 --> 00:03:43,556
<i>‎Just one stood alone.</i>

97
00:03:43,640 --> 00:03:46,226
‎Right,<i>‎ Letters From Exile.</i>

98
00:03:46,309 --> 00:03:50,688
‎Jeong Yak-yong wrote them.

99
00:03:51,397 --> 00:03:52,273
‎How funny.

100
00:03:53,650 --> 00:03:54,734
‎Food's here.

101
00:03:54,817 --> 00:03:57,862
‎Can't they treat us
‎to something tasty just once?

102
00:03:57,946 --> 00:04:01,366
‎Wait a second, that's exactly what I had
‎before I left this place last time.

103
00:04:01,449 --> 00:04:02,825
‎This is the third time
‎we've gotten olive bread.

104
00:04:02,909 --> 00:04:03,993
‎I'll be back.

105
00:04:07,080 --> 00:04:08,790
‎Thank you for the food.

106
00:04:09,874 --> 00:04:14,170
‎Will JAE JAE end up back in the exile zone
‎if she loses in the prison match today?

107
00:04:14,254 --> 00:04:16,130
‎I don't fully understand
‎the system either.

108
00:04:16,798 --> 00:04:18,424
‎You can't leave today.

109
00:04:18,508 --> 00:04:20,218
‎-What?
‎-You can't leave me today.

110
00:04:20,301 --> 00:04:22,303
‎We need to make it to the finals.

111
00:04:22,845 --> 00:04:25,139
‎I wanna be there with you.

112
00:04:29,560 --> 00:04:31,145
‎What's John up to?

113
00:04:31,729 --> 00:04:33,147
‎What is he folding?

114
00:04:36,442 --> 00:04:37,735
‎I'm making cards.

115
00:04:38,903 --> 00:04:39,779
‎To use with this.

116
00:04:40,488 --> 00:04:43,116
‎He's making cards
‎in case a card game comes up.

117
00:04:44,117 --> 00:04:47,537
‎Could that be the secret
‎to his prison match-winning streak?

118
00:04:48,121 --> 00:04:51,207
‎Yeah, he's one resilient guy.

119
00:04:51,708 --> 00:04:53,126
‎What's with the scraps of paper?

120
00:04:53,626 --> 00:04:55,378
‎-We're playing poker.
‎-Poker?

121
00:04:55,461 --> 00:04:56,587
‎I just made the cards.

122
00:04:56,671 --> 00:04:57,714
‎With those as chips?

123
00:04:57,797 --> 00:04:59,465
‎-I'll bet four.
‎-I fold.

124
00:05:00,341 --> 00:05:01,426
‎This is hilarious.

125
00:05:05,471 --> 00:05:07,849
<i>‎I heard about the exile zone,</i>

126
00:05:07,932 --> 00:05:09,225
<i>‎but I was still a bit uneasy</i>

127
00:05:09,309 --> 00:05:12,186
<i>‎because I wasn't sure that system</i>
<i>‎would still be in effect.</i>

128
00:05:12,270 --> 00:05:14,814
‎Had that been the case,
‎I would've felt really wronged.

129
00:05:17,442 --> 00:05:18,985
‎But listen,
‎that doesn't make sense because…

130
00:05:19,068 --> 00:05:19,902
‎-Hey.
‎-What the heck?

131
00:05:19,986 --> 00:05:21,946
‎-This looks like a fun game.
‎-You're done already?

132
00:05:22,030 --> 00:05:23,239
‎-Hey.
‎-What time is it?

133
00:05:24,073 --> 00:05:25,033
‎-The time?
‎-Yeah.

134
00:05:25,116 --> 00:05:26,617
‎-You need to know the time here.
‎-Yeah.

135
00:05:26,701 --> 00:05:29,203
‎You have to go back down if you don't.

136
00:05:29,287 --> 00:05:31,581
‎-Yeah.
‎-It's for player registration later.

137
00:05:31,664 --> 00:05:32,790
‎Yeah.

138
00:05:32,874 --> 00:05:35,001
‎-You need to know the time.
‎-The time you got here.

139
00:05:35,501 --> 00:05:39,047
‎We played a bit to prank the newcomer.

140
00:05:39,130 --> 00:05:41,716
<i>‎We thought hard</i>
<i>‎about how to mess with them.</i>

141
00:05:41,799 --> 00:05:44,302
‎-Quick, go find it out.
‎-You need to know when you got eliminated.

142
00:05:44,385 --> 00:05:45,845
‎Go and ask them what time it was.

143
00:05:45,928 --> 00:05:47,889
‎-Hurry.
‎-How was I supposed to know that?

144
00:05:47,972 --> 00:05:49,140
‎-Go on.
‎-Go and ask them.

145
00:05:49,223 --> 00:05:50,767
‎Will they tell me if I do?

146
00:05:50,850 --> 00:05:52,435
‎I'm already here.

147
00:05:52,518 --> 00:05:54,520
‎As soon as I arrived,
‎they said I had to register.

148
00:05:54,604 --> 00:05:55,855
‎Was it player registration?

149
00:05:55,938 --> 00:05:57,857
‎Dong-jae kept going on
‎about that nonsense.

150
00:05:59,859 --> 00:06:02,320
‎How did you end up here today?

151
00:06:05,740 --> 00:06:07,158
‎-"Today's game
‎-Yeah?

152
00:06:07,241 --> 00:06:09,077
‎-is Hidden Word."
‎-Hidden Word?

153
00:06:09,160 --> 00:06:10,828
‎-That's spot on.
‎-"In Hidden Word,

154
00:06:10,912 --> 00:06:12,914
‎players must choose a word

155
00:06:12,997 --> 00:06:15,833
‎and provide elusive but relevant hints."

156
00:06:15,917 --> 00:06:19,587
‎"Other players must guess
‎the prompter's word to score points."

157
00:06:19,670 --> 00:06:21,547
‎-That's pretty good.
‎-Yeah, it is.

158
00:06:21,631 --> 00:06:22,840
‎That's not what I asked.

159
00:06:22,924 --> 00:06:24,592
‎I just asked him what the game was,

160
00:06:24,675 --> 00:06:26,511
‎but then he suddenly became
‎a game show host.

161
00:06:26,594 --> 00:06:28,304
‎-You could use a Piece
‎-Yeah?

162
00:06:28,387 --> 00:06:30,431
‎to submit two answers.

163
00:06:30,515 --> 00:06:31,933
‎-And everyone had Pieces to spare?
‎-Yeah.

164
00:06:32,016 --> 00:06:34,018
‎JAE JAE actually showed up with ten.

165
00:06:34,102 --> 00:06:35,269
‎-Pieces?
‎-She had ten?

166
00:06:35,353 --> 00:06:37,021
‎-She brought ten with her.
‎-Ten Pieces?

167
00:06:37,105 --> 00:06:38,064
‎No way.

168
00:06:39,732 --> 00:06:42,485
‎She's the revered senior member
‎of the exile zone.

169
00:06:43,111 --> 00:06:45,947
‎She was the living historian
‎of this place.

170
00:06:46,030 --> 00:06:47,198
‎-I see.
‎-Undefeated.

171
00:06:47,281 --> 00:06:48,866
‎So what word did you choose?

172
00:06:48,950 --> 00:06:50,159
‎Let us guess.

173
00:06:50,243 --> 00:06:52,453
‎-"City" was the first hint.
‎-Okay.

174
00:06:52,537 --> 00:06:54,914
‎That got 96.5% right away,
‎so no further hints.

175
00:06:56,290 --> 00:06:57,917
‎Figure out the answer based on "city."

176
00:06:58,000 --> 00:06:58,960
‎"City"?

177
00:06:59,627 --> 00:07:00,878
‎Seoul.

178
00:07:00,962 --> 00:07:02,296
‎Capital.

179
00:07:02,380 --> 00:07:03,422
‎"Seoul"?

180
00:07:03,506 --> 00:07:04,465
‎-Capital.
‎-"Capital"?

181
00:07:04,549 --> 00:07:06,467
‎The answer was capital.

182
00:07:06,551 --> 00:07:08,427
‎-She got it on the first try.
‎-How did you do it?

183
00:07:08,511 --> 00:07:09,345
‎Give us the next one.

184
00:07:09,846 --> 00:07:12,807
‎-Keep going. Come on.
‎-Yeah. It's a good way to pass the time.

185
00:07:12,890 --> 00:07:14,600
‎Give us more. Whatever you got.

186
00:07:14,684 --> 00:07:15,726
‎-"Umbrella."
‎-Okay.

187
00:07:15,810 --> 00:07:17,603
‎-That got 96.5%.
‎-Damn it.

188
00:07:17,687 --> 00:07:19,939
‎-Maybe something like "raincoat."
‎-No, that can't be it.

189
00:07:20,022 --> 00:07:21,399
‎Right, so something like that.

190
00:07:21,482 --> 00:07:22,525
‎"Raincoat" was the answer.

191
00:07:22,608 --> 00:07:24,402
‎-It really was?
‎-Next question.

192
00:07:24,485 --> 00:07:26,571
‎XITSUH gave an insane one.

193
00:07:26,654 --> 00:07:28,364
‎John's one was just as wild.

194
00:07:28,448 --> 00:07:29,949
‎Really? What was it?

195
00:07:30,032 --> 00:07:31,075
‎Tell us the next one.

196
00:07:31,159 --> 00:07:32,493
‎I'm getting a dopamine rush.

197
00:07:32,577 --> 00:07:35,371
‎You learn to cherish stuff like that
‎in this place.

198
00:07:35,455 --> 00:07:36,706
‎-The happenings of others?
‎-Yeah.

199
00:07:37,206 --> 00:07:38,458
‎-They're so precious.
‎-The happenings.

200
00:07:38,541 --> 00:07:40,126
‎-They're so important.
‎-News from the outside.

201
00:07:40,209 --> 00:07:43,754
‎We were totally consumed
‎by that Hidden Word game.

202
00:07:43,838 --> 00:07:45,882
‎Time passed by so quickly.

203
00:07:47,758 --> 00:07:49,760
‎Oh no. It's time.

204
00:07:49,844 --> 00:07:50,803
‎Here we go.

205
00:07:51,596 --> 00:07:53,139
‎The time has come.

206
00:07:53,222 --> 00:07:55,224
‎-It's time now.
‎-It's my first time too.

207
00:07:55,933 --> 00:07:57,852
<i>‎We will now begin the exile zone match.</i>

208
00:07:57,935 --> 00:07:59,061
‎Bring it in first.

209
00:07:59,687 --> 00:08:02,148
‎-Cheer on three.
<i>‎-Please make your way</i>

210
00:08:02,231 --> 00:08:04,567
‎-One, two, three. We got this.
<i>‎-to a spot of your choice.</i>

211
00:08:05,151 --> 00:08:06,861
‎-Let's go.
‎-This is nuts.

212
00:08:06,944 --> 00:08:07,904
‎Let's do this.

213
00:08:07,987 --> 00:08:09,780
‎-Do we stand here?
‎-What is this?

214
00:08:09,864 --> 00:08:10,990
‎-A pen.
‎-What is this?

215
00:08:11,073 --> 00:08:12,241
‎-It's a pen.
‎-There's a pen here.

216
00:08:12,325 --> 00:08:13,451
‎Why is there a pen here?

217
00:08:13,534 --> 00:08:16,412
<i>‎The lowest-ranking player</i>
<i>‎in the exile zone match</i>

218
00:08:16,496 --> 00:08:17,830
<i>‎will go home.</i>

219
00:08:18,664 --> 00:08:21,042
<i>‎The sixth exile zone match is</i>

220
00:08:21,125 --> 00:08:22,335
<i>‎Flags of the World.</i>

221
00:08:22,418 --> 00:08:23,461
‎-What?
‎-"Flags of the World"?

222
00:08:23,544 --> 00:08:26,130
<i>‎First, ten different national flags</i>
<i>‎will be revealed one by one,</i>

223
00:08:26,214 --> 00:08:28,716
<i>‎each for one second.</i>

224
00:08:29,217 --> 00:08:31,302
<i>‎This will be repeated three times</i>
<i>‎in the same order,</i>

225
00:08:31,385 --> 00:08:34,222
<i>‎for a total of 30 seconds.</i>

226
00:08:34,305 --> 00:08:35,640
<i>‎Five seconds later,</i>

227
00:08:35,723 --> 00:08:39,727
<i>‎a set of 25 national flags</i>
<i>‎will be revealed on a single screen.</i>

228
00:08:39,810 --> 00:08:43,606
<i>‎Five of the originally revealed ten flags</i>

229
00:08:43,689 --> 00:08:45,942
<i>‎will be included in this set.</i>

230
00:08:46,025 --> 00:08:47,693
<i>‎Players will have one minute</i>

231
00:08:47,777 --> 00:08:50,488
<i>‎to find the five flags</i>
<i>‎from the original ten</i>

232
00:08:50,571 --> 00:08:53,032
<i>‎and mark them with a circle.</i>

233
00:08:53,115 --> 00:08:54,283
‎This show is just insane.

234
00:08:54,367 --> 00:08:57,578
<i>‎Players will earn one point</i>
<i>‎with each correct answer.</i>

235
00:08:57,662 --> 00:09:00,414
<i>‎The game consists of</i>
<i>‎a total of three rounds,</i>

236
00:09:00,498 --> 00:09:03,960
<i>‎and the player with the fewest points</i>
<i>‎will go home.</i>

237
00:09:04,544 --> 00:09:07,505
<i>‎We will now begin the game.</i>

238
00:09:07,588 --> 00:09:09,507
‎-Do you know your flags?
‎-Not at all.

239
00:09:09,590 --> 00:09:12,301
‎You don't?
‎Oh man, guess we're both screwed.

240
00:09:12,385 --> 00:09:15,846
<i>‎Honestly, I knew it'd be</i>
<i>‎a memory game today.</i>

241
00:09:15,930 --> 00:09:18,766
‎Looking back at the exile zone's history
‎up to this point,

242
00:09:18,849 --> 00:09:22,353
‎it seemed like it had been
‎about three days since the last one.

243
00:09:22,436 --> 00:09:24,272
‎So I thought
‎that it was about time for another.

244
00:09:24,355 --> 00:09:27,149
‎I'm absolutely hopeless
‎when it comes to world flags.

245
00:09:27,233 --> 00:09:29,068
<i>‎I barely know any countries.</i>

246
00:09:29,151 --> 00:09:30,194
<i>‎Before the game started,</i>

247
00:09:30,278 --> 00:09:33,614
<i>‎Won-young joined us</i>
<i>‎and did a whole hosting bit</i>

248
00:09:33,698 --> 00:09:37,410
<i>‎where he basically reenacted the game</i>
<i>‎he played earlier.</i>

249
00:09:37,493 --> 00:09:40,830
‎Seeing him do that
‎made me realize he had a great memory.

250
00:09:40,913 --> 00:09:43,457
<i>‎Round 1 will now begin.</i>

251
00:09:43,541 --> 00:09:45,793
<i>‎Here are the ten flags.</i>

252
00:10:25,041 --> 00:10:28,669
‎ANSWERS WILL BE REVEALED TO VIEWERS FIRST

253
00:10:28,753 --> 00:10:29,920
‎Damn it.

254
00:10:30,004 --> 00:10:32,131
<i>‎I'm not really good with flags,</i>

255
00:10:32,214 --> 00:10:34,884
‎so I thought I'd rely on
‎what little I do know

256
00:10:34,967 --> 00:10:36,552
‎and use that to memorize them.

257
00:10:36,636 --> 00:10:42,683
<i>‎Then I noticed they'd mixed in</i>
<i>‎the flags of Ireland and Côte d'Ivoire.</i>

258
00:11:04,497 --> 00:11:08,334
‎For the flags I knew, I memorized them
‎by the first letter of the country name.

259
00:11:08,417 --> 00:11:09,794
‎For the ones I didn't know,

260
00:11:09,877 --> 00:11:13,172
<i>‎I drilled them into my head, focusing on</i>
<i>‎key features like colors or emblems.</i>

261
00:11:26,310 --> 00:11:28,270
<i>‎Ten seconds remaining.</i>

262
00:11:33,150 --> 00:11:34,985
<i>‎Your time is up.</i>

263
00:11:36,737 --> 00:11:39,115
<i>‎Kim Dong-jae has earned four points.</i>

264
00:11:39,198 --> 00:11:41,283
<i>‎Jung Won-young has earned four points.</i>

265
00:11:41,367 --> 00:11:44,245
<i>‎Yurisa has earned five points.</i>

266
00:11:47,248 --> 00:11:49,625
‎Damn it, so that was right.

267
00:11:51,460 --> 00:11:53,838
‎You can't go into details
‎when it comes to memorization.

268
00:11:53,921 --> 00:11:57,258
‎Just go with whether
‎you like the flag or not when you see it,

269
00:11:57,341 --> 00:12:00,386
‎and when the full board comes up,
‎just pick the ones you like.

270
00:12:00,886 --> 00:12:02,596
<i>‎As the flags flashed by on screen,</i>

271
00:12:02,680 --> 00:12:05,349
<i>‎I thought, "Wow, that flag's pretty.</i>
<i>‎Look at those colors."</i>

272
00:12:05,433 --> 00:12:08,185
<i>‎Then I just chose the ones</i>
<i>‎that I thought were pretty.</i>

273
00:12:09,228 --> 00:12:10,271
‎I'm done.

274
00:12:10,354 --> 00:12:14,108
‎When I saw Yurisa get a perfect score
‎on the very first round,

275
00:12:14,733 --> 00:12:17,903
‎I realized that I shouldn't
‎even dream of first place.

276
00:12:17,987 --> 00:12:20,197
<i>‎I decided to aim for second.</i>

277
00:12:20,281 --> 00:12:22,324
<i>‎Round 2 will now begin.</i>

278
00:12:22,408 --> 00:12:24,577
<i>‎Here are the ten flags.</i>

279
00:12:26,912 --> 00:12:29,623
<i>‎There were some pretty flags</i>
<i>‎this time too.</i>

280
00:12:29,707 --> 00:12:34,253
<i>‎Many had nice shapes or a pretty emblem.</i>

281
00:12:35,838 --> 00:12:39,216
<i>‎I knew I had to rethink my strategy</i>
<i>‎starting with the second round,</i>

282
00:12:39,300 --> 00:12:41,135
<i>‎so I decided to memorize in sentences.</i>

283
00:12:42,386 --> 00:12:44,263
‎C with a star…

284
00:12:47,892 --> 00:12:49,143
‎C with a star…

285
00:12:49,768 --> 00:12:51,520
‎What the hell?

286
00:13:04,241 --> 00:13:06,076
<i>‎There were two that confused me.</i>

287
00:13:06,160 --> 00:13:08,913
<i>‎I don't know what kind of connection</i>
<i>‎the two countries shared,</i>

288
00:13:08,996 --> 00:13:11,165
<i>‎but they had the same colors,</i>
<i>‎just arranged differently.</i>

289
00:13:11,248 --> 00:13:13,417
<i>‎I couldn't remember if the one I saw</i>
<i>‎had red or green on top.</i>

290
00:13:13,501 --> 00:13:17,796
<i>‎I think I wasted a lot of time</i>
<i>‎agonizing over that.</i>

291
00:13:20,382 --> 00:13:22,259
<i>‎Ten seconds remaining.</i>

292
00:13:36,148 --> 00:13:38,067
<i>‎Your time is up.</i>

293
00:13:40,152 --> 00:13:41,362
‎What on earth?

294
00:13:41,445 --> 00:13:43,405
<i>‎Yurisa has earned four points.</i>

295
00:13:43,489 --> 00:13:45,783
<i>‎Jung Won-young has earned three points.</i>

296
00:13:45,866 --> 00:13:48,911
<i>‎Kim Dong-jae has earned three points.</i>

297
00:13:49,411 --> 00:13:52,164
‎I scored three points,
‎and Won-young did as well.

298
00:13:52,248 --> 00:13:54,708
‎I knew it'd come down to Dong-jae and me,

299
00:13:54,792 --> 00:13:57,461
<i>‎but I started to feel the pressure</i>
<i>‎when we tied twice.</i>

300
00:13:57,545 --> 00:13:59,964
<i>‎Round 3 will now begin.</i>

301
00:14:00,047 --> 00:14:02,508
<i>‎Here are the ten flags.</i>

302
00:14:12,935 --> 00:14:15,980
<i>‎My approach was to start</i>
<i>‎with flags I already knew.</i>

303
00:14:16,063 --> 00:14:17,147
<i>‎There were the Dutch flag,</i>

304
00:14:17,231 --> 00:14:18,774
<i>‎a flag that looked Russian,</i>

305
00:14:18,857 --> 00:14:19,900
<i>‎and then the Jamaican one.</i>

306
00:14:19,984 --> 00:14:23,904
<i>‎I thought I was in good shape</i>
<i>‎to secure my survival.</i>

307
00:15:00,608 --> 00:15:02,192
<i>‎Ten seconds remaining.</i>

308
00:15:16,665 --> 00:15:18,751
<i>‎Your time is up.</i>

309
00:15:18,834 --> 00:15:19,919
‎Damn it.

310
00:15:22,630 --> 00:15:25,507
<i>‎Yurisa has scored 13 points total.</i>

311
00:15:25,591 --> 00:15:28,510
<i>‎Kim Dong-jae has scored 11 points total.</i>

312
00:15:28,594 --> 00:15:29,678
<i>‎Jung Won-young…</i>

313
00:15:32,765 --> 00:15:34,683
<i>‎has scored 11 points total.</i>

314
00:15:39,146 --> 00:15:41,482
<i>‎Yurisa, you have survived.</i>

315
00:15:41,565 --> 00:15:43,609
<i>‎Please remain at your spot.</i>

316
00:15:43,692 --> 00:15:46,278
<i>‎Kim Dong-jae and Jung Won-young</i>

317
00:15:46,362 --> 00:15:50,491
<i>‎will play a tiebreaker round</i>
<i>‎to determine who will be eliminated.</i>

318
00:15:53,077 --> 00:15:53,911
<i>‎We tied again.</i>

319
00:15:53,994 --> 00:15:56,372
‎We scored identically for every round.

320
00:15:56,455 --> 00:16:01,126
‎If only I had gotten just one more right,

321
00:16:01,210 --> 00:16:03,420
‎we wouldn't have needed
‎a tiebreaker round.

322
00:16:03,504 --> 00:16:05,005
<i>‎Hearing it was a tie,</i>

323
00:16:05,089 --> 00:16:10,135
<i>‎I became laser-focused,</i>
<i>‎determined to get every single one right.</i>

324
00:16:10,219 --> 00:16:12,805
<i>‎We will now begin the tiebreaker round.</i>

325
00:16:12,888 --> 00:16:15,182
<i>‎Here are the flags.</i>

326
00:16:43,961 --> 00:16:47,172
<i>‎I recognized a lot of them.</i>

327
00:16:55,389 --> 00:16:58,809
<i>‎My palms were so sweaty,</i>
<i>‎and I was about to lose my mind.</i>

328
00:17:08,485 --> 00:17:10,154
<i>‎I needed to survive.</i>

329
00:17:26,920 --> 00:17:28,714
<i>‎Your time is up.</i>

330
00:17:30,716 --> 00:17:32,551
<i>‎Kim Dong-jae has earned four points.</i>

331
00:17:33,052 --> 00:17:34,970
<i>‎Jung Won-young has earned five points.</i>

332
00:17:35,679 --> 00:17:36,930
‎Good job, both of you.

333
00:17:37,014 --> 00:17:38,974
<i>‎That concludes the exile zone match.</i>

334
00:17:39,058 --> 00:17:41,560
<i>‎Farewell, Kim Dong-jae.</i>

335
00:17:41,643 --> 00:17:42,686
‎Good job.

336
00:17:46,356 --> 00:17:47,232
‎I'm off.

337
00:17:48,192 --> 00:17:50,861
‎Man, I thought I'd be here
‎for another day.

338
00:17:50,944 --> 00:17:51,779
‎Bye-bye.

339
00:17:52,279 --> 00:17:53,906
‎I'm really disappointed.

340
00:17:53,989 --> 00:17:55,616
‎I wish I'd done a little better.

341
00:17:55,699 --> 00:17:57,785
<i>‎I wish I could've focused a bit more.</i>

342
00:17:57,868 --> 00:17:59,870
<i>‎But what can I do? I did what I could.</i>

343
00:17:59,953 --> 00:18:02,873
<i>‎So now it's time to go back to my life,</i>

344
00:18:02,956 --> 00:18:06,585
<i>‎regroup in the real world,</i>

345
00:18:06,668 --> 00:18:09,338
‎and live as the best version of myself.

346
00:18:10,089 --> 00:18:12,674
‎Bye, Dong-jae. He got burned.

347
00:18:15,135 --> 00:18:16,678
‎You survived by just one point.

348
00:18:18,472 --> 00:18:20,390
‎Tomorrow's the last day.

349
00:18:20,474 --> 00:18:22,184
‎-Why?
‎-Tomorrow's day six, isn't it?

350
00:18:22,267 --> 00:18:25,229
‎Does that say the sixth day
‎is the last day?

351
00:18:25,312 --> 00:18:27,689
‎Originally, one person can make it back.

352
00:18:27,773 --> 00:18:31,443
‎But as a bonus,
‎if someone can solve that on time,

353
00:18:31,527 --> 00:18:32,528
‎-they can return too.
‎-I see.

354
00:18:32,611 --> 00:18:35,697
‎So that's why
‎one more person got to return.

355
00:18:35,781 --> 00:18:36,907
‎And then on day six,

356
00:18:36,990 --> 00:18:40,035
‎the winner of the final match
‎gets to return.

357
00:18:41,245 --> 00:18:42,371
‎That's insane.

358
00:18:42,996 --> 00:18:45,499
‎You've had the full experience.

359
00:18:45,999 --> 00:18:47,417
‎Starting from the secret room.

360
00:18:47,501 --> 00:18:51,880
‎So right now, it's just Dong-min
‎and Kyung-lyul in the living area?

361
00:18:53,465 --> 00:18:54,633
‎The vibes must be unreal.

362
00:18:55,134 --> 00:18:57,177
‎Today, it's JAE JAE, John,

363
00:18:57,261 --> 00:18:59,179
‎-and XITSUH in prison.
‎-XITSUH.

364
00:18:59,972 --> 00:19:01,098
‎I wonder who will come.

365
00:19:01,181 --> 00:19:02,015
‎Yeah, I wonder.

366
00:19:02,099 --> 00:19:04,810
‎I have a feeling it'll be XITSUH.

367
00:19:04,893 --> 00:19:06,520
‎I hope JAE JAE comes.

368
00:19:06,603 --> 00:19:08,856
‎Why do you say that?

369
00:19:08,939 --> 00:19:11,275
‎-Why would you jinx her?
‎-She has a wealth of knowledge.

370
00:19:11,358 --> 00:19:13,193
‎-You didn't see her here, right?
‎-I did.

371
00:19:13,277 --> 00:19:15,821
‎-Right, you were here yesterday.
‎-Yeah. Briefly, but still.

372
00:19:16,989 --> 00:19:19,366
‎Damn it, I was about to lie down.

373
00:19:20,534 --> 00:19:21,493
‎What is it?

374
00:19:21,577 --> 00:19:25,497
<i>‎The prison match will begin in 30 minutes.</i>

375
00:19:25,581 --> 00:19:28,167
<i>‎Let me introduce the fifth prison match.</i>

376
00:19:28,250 --> 00:19:29,835
‎-Let's go.
‎-It's been a while.

377
00:19:29,918 --> 00:19:31,461
<i>‎Today's prison match is</i>

378
00:19:31,545 --> 00:19:32,796
<i>‎Tower of Equations.</i>

379
00:19:32,880 --> 00:19:34,423
‎-That's the worst.
‎-Equations!

380
00:19:34,506 --> 00:19:36,049
‎I've been doing nothing but arithmetic.

381
00:19:36,133 --> 00:19:37,676
‎So there comes the equation game.

382
00:19:37,759 --> 00:19:38,635
<i>‎In Tower of Equations,</i>

383
00:19:38,719 --> 00:19:41,847
<i>‎players must move number blocks</i>
<i>‎and stack them into a tower</i>

384
00:19:41,930 --> 00:19:44,391
<i>‎to reach the target number.</i>

385
00:19:45,184 --> 00:19:46,685
<i>‎At the start of each round,</i>

386
00:19:46,768 --> 00:19:50,856
<i>‎the target number and target floor count</i>
<i>‎will be revealed on the monitor.</i>

387
00:19:51,481 --> 00:19:52,774
<i>‎The target number</i>

388
00:19:52,858 --> 00:19:56,862
<i>‎is the final result of the equation</i>
<i>‎that must be completed in the round.</i>

389
00:19:56,945 --> 00:19:58,280
<i>‎The target floor count</i>

390
00:19:58,363 --> 00:20:00,657
<i>‎is the number of floors</i>
<i>‎in the equation tower</i>

391
00:20:00,741 --> 00:20:02,618
<i>‎that must be stacked</i>
<i>‎to reach the target number.</i>

392
00:20:02,701 --> 00:20:06,747
<i>‎If the target number is 25</i>
<i>‎and the target floor count is 4,</i>

393
00:20:06,830 --> 00:20:08,457
<i>‎players must stack four number blocks</i>

394
00:20:08,540 --> 00:20:12,669
<i>‎to create an equation tower</i>
<i>‎with a result of 25.</i>

395
00:20:14,129 --> 00:20:15,547
<i>‎Once the prompt is revealed,</i>

396
00:20:15,631 --> 00:20:18,634
<i>‎players will have five minutes</i>
<i>‎to press the buzzer</i>

397
00:20:18,717 --> 00:20:23,263
<i>‎and declare the minimum number of moves</i>
<i>‎needed to complete the target number.</i>

398
00:20:23,972 --> 00:20:26,975
<i>‎A move refers to the action of lifting</i>

399
00:20:27,059 --> 00:20:30,395
<i>‎any number of blocks</i>
<i>‎from the top of a stack</i>

400
00:20:30,479 --> 00:20:33,398
<i>‎and placing them in a desired position.</i>

401
00:20:33,482 --> 00:20:36,526
<i>‎This entire process</i>
<i>‎will count as one move.</i>

402
00:20:37,319 --> 00:20:41,490
<i>‎The lifted blocks</i>
<i>‎can be flipped upside down,</i>

403
00:20:41,573 --> 00:20:45,869
<i>‎and flipping the blocks in the same spot</i>
<i>‎will also count as one move.</i>

404
00:20:46,620 --> 00:20:50,499
<i>‎If a player declares the minimum number</i>
<i>‎of moves within five minutes,</i>

405
00:20:51,124 --> 00:20:54,127
<i>‎the original five-minute time limit</i>
<i>‎will end,</i>

406
00:20:54,211 --> 00:20:58,590
<i>‎and the other players will then be given</i>
<i>‎an additional two minutes.</i>

407
00:20:58,674 --> 00:20:59,967
<i>‎During this time,</i>

408
00:21:00,050 --> 00:21:02,302
<i>‎any player who can complete an equation</i>

409
00:21:02,386 --> 00:21:06,515
<i>‎to reach the target number</i>
<i>‎in fewer moves than the declared number</i>

410
00:21:06,598 --> 00:21:09,977
<i>‎may declare a new minimum move count.</i>

411
00:21:10,060 --> 00:21:14,356
<i>‎However, the minimum move count</i>
<i>‎may only be declared once by each player.</i>

412
00:21:15,357 --> 00:21:17,150
<i>‎After the additional time ends,</i>

413
00:21:17,234 --> 00:21:20,112
<i>‎only the player who declared</i>
<i>‎the fewest moves</i>

414
00:21:20,195 --> 00:21:21,947
<i>‎will proceed to move the blocks.</i>

415
00:21:23,573 --> 00:21:25,909
<i>‎The player will then have two minutes</i>

416
00:21:25,993 --> 00:21:29,579
<i>‎to move the blocks</i>
<i>‎exactly the number of times they declared,</i>

417
00:21:29,663 --> 00:21:32,791
<i>‎completing an equation tower</i>
<i>‎with the target floor count</i>

418
00:21:32,874 --> 00:21:34,084
<i>‎that equals the target number.</i>

419
00:21:34,918 --> 00:21:38,046
<i>‎The top-floor block of the equation tower</i>

420
00:21:38,130 --> 00:21:41,341
<i>‎must be a number with no operator symbol,</i>

421
00:21:41,425 --> 00:21:45,429
<i>‎and the equation will be read</i>
<i>‎from top to bottom.</i>

422
00:21:47,055 --> 00:21:48,473
<i>‎If the player completes an equation</i>

423
00:21:48,557 --> 00:21:50,976
<i>‎that meets the target floor count</i>
<i>‎and target number</i>

424
00:21:51,059 --> 00:21:53,770
<i>‎after declaring their move count</i>
<i>‎within the initial five minutes,</i>

425
00:21:53,854 --> 00:21:55,772
<i>‎they will earn one point.</i>

426
00:21:56,398 --> 00:21:59,443
<i>‎If they fail, one point will be deducted.</i>

427
00:22:00,861 --> 00:22:05,949
<i>‎If a player who declared a lower count</i>
<i>‎during the additional time succeeds,</i>

428
00:22:06,033 --> 00:22:07,242
<i>‎they will earn two points.</i>

429
00:22:08,201 --> 00:22:11,121
