1128
00:54:48,451 --> 00:54:50,996
‎There's an eyeball, symbols,
‎and all sorts of stuff here.

1129
00:54:51,579 --> 00:54:56,876
‎Everything here is a clue
‎for solving the hidden stage.

1130
00:54:56,960 --> 00:54:58,628
‎-But JAE JAE already solved it.
‎-Yeah.

1131
00:54:58,712 --> 00:55:01,256
‎-So there's nothing to solve.
‎-All of this is solved already, right?

1132
00:55:01,339 --> 00:55:02,173
‎Yeah.

1133
00:55:02,757 --> 00:55:04,718
‎-It's all done.
‎-Okay.

1134
00:55:06,302 --> 00:55:07,303
‎Wait, what?

1135
00:55:08,138 --> 00:55:09,848
‎-We're going right into it?
‎-Seriously?

1136
00:55:09,931 --> 00:55:12,350
<i>‎We will now begin the exile zone match.</i>

1137
00:55:12,434 --> 00:55:15,311
‎At the end of the game, one of us will be…

1138
00:55:15,395 --> 00:55:17,522
‎-Sent off without a chance to say goodbye.
‎-Okay.

1139
00:55:17,605 --> 00:55:18,648
‎It's been fun.

1140
00:55:19,315 --> 00:55:20,692
‎I'm off. It's been fun.

1141
00:55:21,484 --> 00:55:23,403
‎At least I got to see this place
‎before leaving.

1142
00:55:23,903 --> 00:55:27,282
<i>‎Please make your way</i>
<i>‎to a spot of your choice.</i>

1143
00:55:29,951 --> 00:55:31,369
‎-Good luck.
‎-Good luck.

1144
00:55:31,453 --> 00:55:34,247
<i>‎The lowest-ranking player</i>
<i>‎in the exile zone match</i>

1145
00:55:34,330 --> 00:55:36,082
<i>‎will go home.</i>

1146
00:55:37,167 --> 00:55:39,085
<i>‎The seventh exile zone match is</i>

1147
00:55:39,961 --> 00:55:41,254
<i>‎Count the Rectangles.</i>

1148
00:55:42,047 --> 00:55:42,881
‎Damn it.

1149
00:55:42,964 --> 00:55:44,799
<i>‎Once the board is revealed,</i>

1150
00:55:44,883 --> 00:55:47,594
<i>‎players must figure out</i>
<i>‎how many rectangular formations</i>

1151
00:55:47,677 --> 00:55:51,973
<i>‎reach the target number</i>
<i>‎when their numbers are added up.</i>

1152
00:55:52,057 --> 00:55:54,434
<i>‎Once a player determines</i>
<i>‎the total number of rectangles,</i>

1153
00:55:54,517 --> 00:55:57,729
<i>‎they can press the buzzer</i>
<i>‎and give their answer within ten seconds.</i>

1154
00:55:57,812 --> 00:55:59,689
<i>‎If the answer is incorrect,</i>

1155
00:55:59,773 --> 00:56:03,610
<i>‎the player cannot attempt</i>
<i>‎the same question again.</i>

1156
00:56:03,693 --> 00:56:06,863
<i>‎There will be a five-minute time limit</i>
<i>‎for every question.</i>

1157
00:56:06,946 --> 00:56:09,866
<i>‎If no player gets the correct answer</i>
<i>‎within the time limit</i>

1158
00:56:09,949 --> 00:56:12,035
<i>‎or if all players get it wrong,</i>

1159
00:56:12,118 --> 00:56:14,329
<i>‎the next question will be presented.</i>

1160
00:56:14,412 --> 00:56:15,872
<i>‎If a player answers correctly,</i>

1161
00:56:15,955 --> 00:56:17,916
<i>‎their survival</i>
<i>‎will be immediately confirmed,</i>

1162
00:56:17,999 --> 00:56:19,667
<i>‎and they will be exempt from the game.</i>

1163
00:56:19,751 --> 00:56:24,214
<i>‎The last remaining player will go home.</i>

1164
00:56:24,297 --> 00:56:26,883
‎We played this on day one.
‎Was it the first game we played?

1165
00:56:26,966 --> 00:56:29,052
<i>‎How funny is it that the first game</i>
<i>‎we played might be our last?</i>

1166
00:56:29,761 --> 00:56:31,012
<i>‎It was the worst.</i>

1167
00:56:31,721 --> 00:56:33,640
<i>‎Even though I've already played that game,</i>

1168
00:56:34,140 --> 00:56:36,976
‎the logic still doesn't make sense to me.

1169
00:56:37,060 --> 00:56:39,771
‎I was fine with it

1170
00:56:39,854 --> 00:56:42,315
‎because I was pretty confident
‎with games involving counting.

1171
00:56:42,398 --> 00:56:45,193
<i>‎I thought, at the very least,</i>
<i>‎I wouldn't come in last.</i>

1172
00:56:45,276 --> 00:56:47,529
‎Okay, I can do this. One last game.

1173
00:56:48,279 --> 00:56:49,739
‎Focus. I can do this.

1174
00:56:49,823 --> 00:56:52,659
<i>‎We will now begin the game.</i>

1175
00:56:52,742 --> 00:56:54,577
<i>‎Here is the game board.</i>

1176
00:57:06,923 --> 00:57:09,425
<i>‎I only had to get it right once,</i>

1177
00:57:09,509 --> 00:57:11,427
<i>‎and without Dong-min,</i>
<i>‎there was no star player.</i>

1178
00:57:11,511 --> 00:57:13,513
<i>‎So I decided to take it slow,</i>
<i>‎without making any mistakes.</i>

1179
00:57:14,806 --> 00:57:17,684
<i>‎I noticed the numbers from 1 to 20</i>

1180
00:57:17,767 --> 00:57:21,020
<i>‎alternated between positive and negative,</i>

1181
00:57:21,104 --> 00:57:24,566
<i>‎so any 2 consecutive numbers</i>
<i>‎would add up to either +1 or -1.</i>

1182
00:57:24,649 --> 00:57:26,151
<i>‎To make zero,</i>

1183
00:57:26,234 --> 00:57:28,778
<i>‎you had to group the pairs.</i>

1184
00:57:36,578 --> 00:57:37,662
‎Two.

1185
00:57:39,789 --> 00:57:40,748
‎Three.

1186
00:57:41,666 --> 00:57:42,500
‎Four.

1187
00:57:44,043 --> 00:57:46,379
‎Five, six, seven, eight.

1188
00:57:48,923 --> 00:57:50,133
‎Twelve.

1189
00:57:56,556 --> 00:57:57,557
<i>‎Jung Won-young.</i>

1190
00:58:01,811 --> 00:58:02,770
‎Twenty-four.

1191
00:58:04,939 --> 00:58:06,024
<i>‎Correct.</i>

1192
00:58:06,107 --> 00:58:08,359
<i>‎You have survived.</i>

1193
00:58:08,443 --> 00:58:10,361
‎-Congrats.
<i>‎-Please remain at your spot.</i>

1194
00:58:11,196 --> 00:58:13,573
<i>‎First, I counted the two-by-two squares</i>

1195
00:58:13,656 --> 00:58:16,284
<i>‎in which +1 and -1</i>
<i>‎could be paired to make 0.</i>

1196
00:58:17,035 --> 00:58:19,162
<i>‎Then the rectangles</i>
<i>‎that could be made with eight squares.</i>

1197
00:58:21,289 --> 00:58:22,207
‎Sixteen.

1198
00:58:22,790 --> 00:58:24,959
<i>‎And the 2 large squares</i>
<i>‎you can make with 16 squares.</i>

1199
00:58:25,043 --> 00:58:27,212
<i>‎Then I just added them all up.</i>

1200
00:58:29,547 --> 00:58:33,301
<i>‎The one among the remaining two players</i>
<i>‎who fails to answer correctly</i>

1201
00:58:33,384 --> 00:58:34,802
<i>‎will go home.</i>

1202
00:58:35,303 --> 00:58:36,846
<i>‎Here is the next game board.</i>

1203
00:58:41,267 --> 00:58:44,395
‎Come on. Please, brain.
‎Just start working already.

1204
00:58:44,479 --> 00:58:48,274
<i>‎I told myself to pull it together</i>
<i>‎and that I had to survive this game.</i>

1205
00:58:49,150 --> 00:58:50,818
<i>‎The last digits were a big help,</i>

1206
00:58:50,902 --> 00:58:55,323
<i>‎so I tried adding those first,</i>
<i>‎then the first digits.</i>

1207
00:58:57,659 --> 00:59:01,162
<i>‎The moment I saw it, I questioned</i>
<i>‎whether it was even made to be added up.</i>

1208
00:59:01,246 --> 00:59:05,041
<i>‎The highest number was 51.</i>
<i>‎How can you make 203 with 3 squares?</i>

1209
00:59:11,381 --> 00:59:12,465
<i>‎XITSUH.</i>

1210
00:59:16,469 --> 00:59:17,387
‎Zero.

1211
00:59:19,347 --> 00:59:20,473
<i>‎Correct.</i>

1212
00:59:20,557 --> 00:59:22,642
<i>‎You have survived.</i>

1213
00:59:25,937 --> 00:59:28,481
<i>‎That concludes the exile zone match.</i>

1214
00:59:28,565 --> 00:59:30,775
<i>‎Farewell, Yurisa.</i>

1215
00:59:33,152 --> 00:59:34,320
‎Take care.

1216
00:59:35,029 --> 00:59:37,448
<i>‎I was really torn about</i>
<i>‎whether I should come on the show,</i>

1217
00:59:37,532 --> 00:59:39,075
<i>‎but I'm glad I did.</i>

1218
00:59:39,158 --> 00:59:42,745
<i>‎It felt like a crash course in life.</i>

1219
00:59:42,829 --> 00:59:47,959
<i>‎This space and the show</i>
<i>‎felt like a microcosm of life itself.</i>

1220
00:59:48,042 --> 00:59:50,336
<i>‎And I realized there's still so much</i>
<i>‎I have to learn in life.</i>

1221
00:59:50,420 --> 00:59:54,841
‎I thought I'd already experienced
‎my fair share of twists and turns in life,

1222
00:59:55,425 --> 00:59:56,968
‎but this was on a different level.

1223
00:59:57,051 --> 00:59:59,554
‎It was just one twist after another.

1224
00:59:59,637 --> 01:00:01,639
‎That's how I'd sum up my time here.

1225
01:00:03,099 --> 01:00:06,352
<i>‎The final match</i>
<i>‎will take place tomorrow morning.</i>

1226
01:00:07,020 --> 01:00:11,649
<i>‎The winner will return to the game area</i>

1227
01:00:11,733 --> 01:00:14,652
<i>‎and once again become a player</i>
<i>‎in</i>‎ The Devil's Plan.

1228
01:00:15,361 --> 01:00:17,238
<i>‎May luck be on your side.</i>

1229
01:00:20,325 --> 01:00:22,118
‎Man, this isn't easy.

1230
01:00:22,744 --> 01:00:27,582
‎Since XITSUH is such a skilled player,
‎we're likely to be evenly matched.

1231
01:00:27,665 --> 01:00:30,627
<i>‎It's now time for me to play</i>
<i>‎just for myself.</i>

1232
01:00:33,338 --> 01:00:34,547
<i>‎I wanna survive.</i>

1233
01:00:34,631 --> 01:00:35,715
<i>‎I do.</i>

1234
01:00:35,798 --> 01:00:38,217
‎The finish line is now in sight.

1235
01:00:38,301 --> 01:00:41,929
<i>‎We have the final match tomorrow morning,</i>

1236
01:00:42,013 --> 01:00:45,266
<i>‎and the winner gets a fresh start.</i>

1237
01:00:46,517 --> 01:00:50,104
‎I need to steel myself
‎to make sure that person is me.

1238
01:00:50,188 --> 01:00:51,272
‎I need to lock in.

1239
01:00:52,857 --> 01:00:55,360
‎Now there's no one left here
‎to explain this setup to us.

1240
01:00:56,152 --> 01:00:57,695
‎We both just came today.

1241
01:00:57,779 --> 01:01:00,782
‎All of this has been passed down
‎by word of mouth.

1242
01:01:03,034 --> 01:01:04,369
‎Do they just keep the lights on?

1243
01:01:04,452 --> 01:01:05,578
‎They said the lights go off

1244
01:01:06,204 --> 01:01:07,997
‎when it's nighttime.

1245
01:01:10,458 --> 01:01:12,126
‎-There we go. It's nighttime.
‎-Like this?

1246
01:01:12,210 --> 01:01:13,378
‎It's nighttime now?

1247
01:01:13,461 --> 01:01:15,505
‎They said you can sleep
‎when the moon is blue.

1248
01:01:16,964 --> 01:01:18,925
‎We still managed to catch the last train.

1249
01:01:19,926 --> 01:01:20,843
‎Did you see this?

1250
01:01:20,927 --> 01:01:23,596
‎We have Shindong's cup,
‎Stella Jang's cup, and so on.

1251
01:01:23,680 --> 01:01:26,099
‎-Oh, the cups of those who came before.
‎-Yeah.

1252
01:01:26,974 --> 01:01:28,184
‎Oh, the cups are named.

1253
01:01:28,267 --> 01:01:29,519
‎Is there one for me too?

1254
01:01:31,312 --> 01:01:32,230
‎It's already here.

1255
01:01:34,482 --> 01:01:36,025
‎Great. Here's what we'll do.

1256
01:01:36,109 --> 01:01:38,403
‎We're adding Yurisa's cup
‎to the collection.

1257
01:01:38,486 --> 01:01:40,613
‎-As a gravestone?
‎-Yeah.

1258
01:01:40,697 --> 01:01:41,572
‎Cup gravestone.

1259
01:01:41,656 --> 01:01:43,616
‎-No, gravestone cup.
‎-Gravestone cup.

1260
01:01:43,700 --> 01:01:44,992
‎Safe journey, Yurisa.

1261
01:01:45,618 --> 01:01:46,619
‎Enjoy this drink.

1262
01:01:48,996 --> 01:01:50,248
‎I'm so tired.

1263
01:01:51,082 --> 01:01:52,417
‎I don't even have the energy to shower.

1264
01:01:54,293 --> 01:01:55,503
‎I survived.

1265
01:01:59,257 --> 01:02:00,633
‎Let's survive tomorrow too.

1266
01:02:18,109 --> 01:02:19,193
‎Is that chicken?

1267
01:02:21,487 --> 01:02:23,656
‎Thank you so much.

1268
01:02:23,740 --> 01:02:25,992
‎Thank you so much for the protein.

1269
01:02:26,075 --> 01:02:28,369
‎Did you put in a special order for us?

1270
01:02:28,453 --> 01:02:31,581
‎There was shredded chicken
‎on top of the porridge.

1271
01:02:31,664 --> 01:02:33,166
‎I was confused.

1272
01:02:33,249 --> 01:02:35,001
‎We've never received such a meal before.

1273
01:02:35,084 --> 01:02:36,753
‎I licked that bowl clean.

1274
01:02:36,836 --> 01:02:38,671
‎Thank you.

1275
01:02:40,339 --> 01:02:43,134
‎There'll probably be a prize match today.

1276
01:02:43,634 --> 01:02:45,762
‎-We failed two, didn't we?
‎-Right.

1277
01:02:45,845 --> 01:02:47,305
‎And we got that one.

1278
01:02:47,388 --> 01:02:49,265
‎-Two went up in flames.
‎-Yeah.

1279
01:02:49,348 --> 01:02:51,559
‎We lost our chance with two of them,
‎if I remember correctly.

1280
01:02:51,642 --> 01:02:55,104
‎-One was the greater good choice.
‎-Right.

1281
01:02:55,188 --> 01:02:56,856
‎-And one in the stocks game.
‎-Right.

1282
01:02:56,939 --> 01:02:58,858
‎So there's one left now.

1283
01:02:58,941 --> 01:03:02,737
‎If there's no mention
‎of a prize match today…

1284
01:03:02,820 --> 01:03:06,115
‎JAE JAE said there was a mission
‎in the exile zone, right?

1285
01:03:06,199 --> 01:03:09,952
‎There was probably prize money
‎involved in that mission.

1286
01:03:10,036 --> 01:03:11,579
‎After finishing the hidden stage,

1287
01:03:11,662 --> 01:03:14,582
‎I was offered to raise the prize money
‎or get Pieces, and I took the Pieces.

1288
01:03:14,665 --> 01:03:15,833
‎There we go.

1289
01:03:15,917 --> 01:03:17,794
‎Here's our villain.

1290
01:03:18,586 --> 01:03:21,798
‎Villain? Come on, I chose greater good,
‎and that was the start of my despair.

1291
01:03:21,881 --> 01:03:23,466
‎Yeah, you have a point.

1292
01:03:23,549 --> 01:03:26,385
‎I needed the Pieces if I was coming back.
‎How else could I survive?

1293
01:03:27,136 --> 01:03:29,347
‎The rest of you have Pieces.

1294
01:03:29,430 --> 01:03:32,058
‎I'm the only one with none.

1295
01:03:32,642 --> 01:03:34,477
‎It's gonna be a tough day for me.

1296
01:03:34,560 --> 01:03:39,649
‎Only one person from the main match today
‎will go straight to the finals.

1297
01:03:39,732 --> 01:03:44,278
<i>‎Everyone's going into the game</i>
<i>‎with a decent amount of Pieces,</i>

1298
01:03:44,362 --> 01:03:48,199
‎but I'm the only one
‎going in with none at all.

1299
01:03:48,282 --> 01:03:51,244
‎So I think the chances
‎of me coming in first are very slim.

1300
01:03:51,327 --> 01:03:52,161
‎With that in mind,

1301
01:03:52,245 --> 01:03:55,039
‎my goal is to win the prison match
‎that comes after

1302
01:03:55,122 --> 01:03:59,752
‎and secure the second spot in the finals.

1303
01:03:59,836 --> 01:04:02,547
‎On a day like today,
‎individual strategy matters a lot

1304
01:04:02,630 --> 01:04:04,257
‎because there's one more chance.

1305
01:04:04,340 --> 01:04:07,468
‎-The main match and the prison match.
‎-Right.

1306
01:04:07,552 --> 01:04:10,805
‎If you're not gonna come in last
‎but also not first,

1307
01:04:10,888 --> 01:04:13,683
‎then you need to figure out
‎who you can beat there to come in first.

1308
01:04:13,766 --> 01:04:15,977
‎-Right.
‎-That's what you need to think about.

1309
01:04:16,060 --> 01:04:18,688
‎How do you think the rest stack up?

1310
01:04:18,771 --> 01:04:20,523
‎Based on how they played yesterday,

1311
01:04:21,190 --> 01:04:25,152
‎everyone who's left
‎seems pretty evenly matched.

1312
01:04:25,236 --> 01:04:28,197
‎It may not all be the same,
‎but everyone here has their strengths.

1313
01:04:28,281 --> 01:04:32,076
‎John has made it through
‎every single prison match.

1314
01:04:32,159 --> 01:04:37,164
<i>‎JAE JAE came back</i>
<i>‎after surviving the brutal exile zone.</i>

1315
01:04:37,248 --> 01:04:39,208
‎Kyung-lyul, in a way,

1316
01:04:39,292 --> 01:04:42,628
<i>‎presented himself as a lone wolf,</i>

1317
01:04:42,712 --> 01:04:45,298
<i>‎which could've made him</i>
<i>‎seem like an underdog.</i>

1318
01:04:45,381 --> 01:04:49,051
‎But he pushed through all of that
‎and made it this far.

1319
01:04:49,552 --> 01:04:52,513
‎John, let's make the finals
‎an underdog revolution.

1320
01:04:52,597 --> 01:04:53,431
‎Sounds good.

1321
01:04:53,514 --> 01:04:55,266
‎Just imagine it.

1322
01:04:55,349 --> 01:04:59,812
‎A newbie facing the survival god Dong-min
‎in the finals.

1323
01:04:59,896 --> 01:05:03,149
‎That alone would be
‎a huge career achievement.

1324
01:05:03,232 --> 01:05:05,651
‎If I make it to the finals,

1325
01:05:05,735 --> 01:05:09,614
‎there's a good chance
‎I'll be going up against Dong-min.

1326
01:05:09,697 --> 01:05:12,033
‎I think you'd need to come in first
‎at least once

1327
01:05:12,116 --> 01:05:14,577
‎to deserve a spot in the finals.

1328
01:05:14,660 --> 01:05:17,288
‎So for today's main match,

1329
01:05:17,371 --> 01:05:19,665
‎my goal isn't just survival
‎but first place.

1330
01:06:03,292 --> 01:06:05,878
‎Let's go.

1331
01:06:05,962 --> 01:06:08,839
‎-No way.
<i>‎-The main match will begin shortly.</i>

1332
01:06:08,923 --> 01:06:12,134
<i>‎Everyone, please gather in the game area.</i>

1333
01:06:12,927 --> 01:06:14,512
‎-We got this.
‎-We got this!

1334
01:06:15,513 --> 01:06:16,430
‎Let's go.

1335
01:06:16,514 --> 01:06:17,431
‎Go!

1336
01:06:26,482 --> 01:06:28,317
‎-Did you sleep well?
